#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048297 :topic/difficulty 0.9052140521889347 :topic/encompasses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186428267 :encompassing/rationale "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 1 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction = 1. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1 (1/1). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: False. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/foundations-frequency-estimates.json, pair 147->1167. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json." :encompassing/topic {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050163} :encompassing/weight 1.0}] :topic/id #uuid "924ef64e-2ec2-5e7b-b9f0-4c335eceb3fb" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059746 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059555 :question/id #uuid "04e1822f-2da1-5b28-8967-7a0026c39319" :question/math-academy-id "e-4401" :question/problem "Find $AB$ and $BA,$ if \n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\nand\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1\\cdot 0+0\\cdot (-1) & 1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 2 \\\\ -5\\cdot 0+1\\cdot (-1) & -5\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-5) & 0\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 1 \\\\ -1\\cdot 1+2\\cdot (-5) & -1\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 1 \\\\ -11 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Watch out!** Notice that \n\n$$\nAB \\neq BA.\n$$\n\nMatrix multiplication is not **commutative**, meaning that when we switch the order of multiplication, we often get a different result (like we did in this example)."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dbfd5f3-553b-5276-8716-bbceddefc4d3" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying 2x2 Square Matrices"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059747 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059556 :question/id #uuid "3b0c400c-89bd-504d-87c3-e0f24957d42b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4402" :question/problem "Find $AB$, if \n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\nand\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0+0-9 & -6+0-3 & 4+0+6 \\\\ 0-1+6 & 9+2+2 & -6-4-4 \\\\ 0+0+3 & -6+0+1 & 4+0-2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -9 & 10 \\\\ 5 & 13 & -14 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c7a77cf-163a-542a-b4a3-4274344b9cf8" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying 3x3 Square Matrices"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059800 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059599 :question/id #uuid "4aaa04dd-1380-50c9-8118-52f6e414f830" :question/math-academy-id "e-5255" :question/problem "Let $Z=XY.$ What is the value of $z_{32}$, if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$X=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$Y=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the $3$rd row in $X$ by the $2$nd column in $Y$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}_{32} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot 4+3\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-1+8-6 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a827b0d0-faa2-521f-b166-e13873b1da00" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Entry of the Product of Two Matrices"}] :topic/math-academy-id 147 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049008} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049125}] :topic/title "Multiplying Square Matrices"}]}
